  "notes": "Strict 1:1 with field_data_tool.R:287-338. Elevation is the site's elevation: the portal reads it from the stations table (calculation_functions.R:93, getRows(pool, 'stations', name == station, columns = c('order','elevation'))). stations.elevation is nullable and calculation_functions.R:96 guards on !any(is.na(c(elev, temp))), so elevation_m is optional: without it Field_BP_altitude is not computed and calcCO2corr can still correct through an in-range Field_BP (`no_elevation_in_range_field_bp_still_corrects`) or return NA (`no_elevation_and_out_of_range_field_bp_omits_co2`). river-data has no site elevation attribute to resolve it from, so the operator types it; that is the tool's one input with no portal-side counterpart. No constants are consumed. Pressure precedence is calcCO2corr's own (calculation_functions.R:126-141): an in-range Field_BP (700-1050 hPa) wins, otherwise Field_BP_altitude; `co2_trio_field_bp_in_range_wins` pins the first branch (its altitude pressure is 959, distinct from the 1000 used) and `co2_trio_field_bp_out_of_range_uses_altitude` the second. The standard curve is the portal's 'Vaisala std curve corr?' checkbox plus curve selector (field_data_tool.R:29,36-51,157-172): present curve => raw * a + b applied to all three columns before the pressure/temperature correction. The portal also writes vaisala_std_curve_id back onto the row (field_data_tool.R:365); that is provenance, which river-data records on the sample instead, so it is not a tool output and carries no pin. The portal's 'KEEP OLD' carry-forward (field_data_tool.R:293-304, reusing the stored Reach_depth_avg_cm/sd when the new value is uncomputable) is out of scope: these tools are stateless, so an uncomputable value is omitted instead, which `reach_depth_single_has_no_sd` and `reach_depths_none_supplied_omits_both` pin. Reach depth replicates are the portal's fixed Reach_depth_rep_1..10 family (tool_field_info.html:17), one param per column, so the replicate a measurement belongs to travels in the field name (`reach_depth_rep_7_measured_alone`) and an unfilled cell is a hole rather than a shift (`reach_depths_gap_in_the_middle`). calcMean/calcSd use na.rm = TRUE, so unfilled replicates drop out of both statistics. There is no eleventh replicate to reject: a name outside the family is refused by the engine as an undeclared param."
}
